{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>YHWH, slow to anger.</b> He did not mention <b>El</b> here, because it connotes strength and might, and He did not wish to show His power against Israel. <b>Gracious and compassionate</b> — he did not mention them because they pertain to a gift, as it is written: ״וצדיק חונן ונותן״, and He was not asking Him to graciously give them anything, but rather to forgive them. <b>And truth</b> — he did not wish to mention it, because he was asking before HaKadosh Baruch Hu to act for them beyond the line of justice, and <b>truth</b> connotes the line of justice, as we say: Torah, about which <b>truth</b> is written — HaKadosh Baruch Hu does not act in it beyond the line of justice. Another interpretation: he did not mention <b>truth</b> — he did not want HaKadosh Baruch Hu to fulfill what He said: ״אכנו בדבר״ etc. <b>Preserving lovingkindness</b> — he did not mention it because they did not perform lovingkindness that He should preserve for them; rather, they transgressed." "<b>And sin.</b> He did not mention it, because it is a term for inadvertent error, as it is written: ״וחטאה בשגגה״, and they acted intentionally and transgressed."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:58.205610733Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}